# TRL — environment variables for local development.
#
# IMPORTANT — what this file does and does not reach:
#
#   * `PUBLIC_*` variables are readable as `import.meta.env.PUBLIC_*` in Astro
#     code, and Vite loads them from here for `astro dev`, `astro build`, and
#     `astro preview`. A real environment variable of the same name takes
#     precedence over this file.
#   * `PUBLIC_SITE_URL` is the exception: `astro.config.mjs` reads it from
#     `process.env` while the config is evaluated, which happens BEFORE Vite
#     loads this file. Setting it here has no effect on a build. Export it in
#     the shell instead, or set it as a build variable on the hosting platform —
#     you can verify what the build will use by running `npm run preflight`.
#
#   * Runtime (server-side) variables are deliberately NOT listed here: the
#     Worker reads them from its own binding environment, which locally means
#     `.dev.vars` (copy `.dev.vars.example` to `.dev.vars`). Never put real
#     credentials in `.env` or `.dev.vars` (docs/TRL_SECURITY.md).

# Canonical origin for the build: canonical URLs, Open Graph URLs, the sitemap,
# and robots.txt all derive from it. Required for a build — there is no default,
# because the intended domain is not owned (D-021).
#
#   export PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:4321"                    # local
#   export PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://trl-service.<sub>.workers.dev"    # interim preview
#   export PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://<real-domain>"                    # live domain
#
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:4321"

# Whether search engines may index this build (D-022). Only the exact value
# "true" turns indexing on; unset, "false", or anything else keeps every page
# noindex and keeps the sitemap out of robots.txt. Set it to "true" when the real
# domain goes live — not while the site is on a temporary workers.dev host.
#
# PUBLIC_ALLOW_INDEXING="false"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime variables (set on the hosting platform; locally these live in
# .dev.vars, not here). Listed for reference — see docs/TRL_DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
#   PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY   Turnstile sitekey rendered into the contact form
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET           Turnstile secret, verified server-side
#   RESEND_API_KEY             Resend API key for enquiry delivery
#   CONTACT_TO_EMAIL           Approved destination (D-003)
#   RESEND_FROM_EMAIL          Verified sender address
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
